"""Agent-authored scientific assessments by /root/primary_a for exact batch A cases; 2026-11-08."""
# index: (disposition, scientific reasoning, exact missing requirement)
ASSESSMENTS={
0:('stock_product_mixture_context','JCM 574 explicitly adds 5 ml of a 1 M NH4Cl solution after cooling. The frozen flat ingredient value 5 G_PER_L loses the volume unit and stock boundary. A source-qualified 1 M ammonium chloride stock is justified; pure NH4Cl is only its solute.',None),
1:('malformed_or_nonchemical_token','Both CCAP K and K35 place this wording in the preparation instruction under Tris stock, not in an ingredient row. Current primary PDFs give the instruction without an acid name after “with”; the frozen 2 MOLAR value does not turn the sentence into a substance. Correct the source extraction and retain this raw token only as provenance.',None),
2:('stock_product_mixture_context','The three chopped-meat source recipes use fat-free ground beef as a heterogeneous animal tissue preparation. They are neither beef extract nor a single purified nutrient. The source-specific removal of fat and subsequent meat processing must remain attached to each recipe; no exact alias to a generic beef ingredient is supported.', 'Compare each original ATCC chopped-meat preparation, including defatting/cooking and any permitted tissue substitutions, before asserting one reusable supplied-material owner.'),
3:('unresolved','NBRC 1284 itself prints sodium acetate·6H2O, 400 mg, so this is not merely a CultureMech punctuation error. Replacing six waters by the familiar trihydrate would contradict the cited source. Its frozen 400 G_PER_L also loses the original milligram unit.', 'An NBRC correction, original formulation, or supplier catalogue/CAS identifying the material called sodium acetate·6H2O in NBRC1284 is needed; do not substitute trihydrate.'),
4:('stock_product_mixture_context','JCM 631 fully identifies Hunter’s basal salts as an NTA/mineral/vitamin stock, with Metals44 and pH adjustment, used at 20 ml. It differs compositionally from JCM900/979 Hutner stocks, including MgSO4 and CaCl2 amounts and vitamins. Propose a separately named JCM631 stock with explicit source partonomy.',None),
5:('existing_identity_or_alias','The TOGO primary JSON for both M2423 and M2422 expands the exact component_name YE through GMO_001003 to Yeast extract. This resolves the abbreviation within both assigned recipes without inferring a supplier product, extract composition or role. The active Yeast_Extract owner is the matching generic ingredient.',None),
6:('stock_product_mixture_context','TOGO M2553 uses 2m HCl to adjust pH and labels it hydrochloric acid solution; it does not supply conc_unit metadata or define whether lowercase m denotes molarity or molality. Preserve the titrant solution and its raw strength notation, separate from pure hydrogen chloride.', 'Obtain the original ATCC formulation or a correction establishing the meaning of “2m” and the actual solution strength; do not silently change m to M.'),
7:('unresolved','TOGO M3254 retains cysteine hydrochloride hydrate but supplies neither L/D/DL stereochemistry nor a water number. The nearby CHEBI91248 owner is specifically L-cysteine hydrochloride monohydrate. Shared cysteine/HCl/hydrate words do not resolve these omitted identity dimensions.', 'Supplier/CAS or an original MB-medium formulation must specify cysteine stereochemistry and hydration number before selecting CHEBI91248 or another form.'),
8:('unresolved','This source-name case combines incompatible preparation scopes: JCM1267 adds 88.8 ml of 10% Fe2(SO4)3 in 0.01 N H2SO4, while NBRC239 lists a 0.005 g ferric sulfate ingredient. The flat JCM occurrence has lost both percentage/solvent and ml. Do not add Fe2(SO4)3 as a universal pure-substance alias across this case.', 'Split the JCM1267/MediaDive5407 prepared-solution occurrences from the NBRC239 and TOGO M3240 material occurrences; confirm percentage basis and salt hydration for each before source-specific mapping.'),
9:('existing_identity_or_alias','JCM552 explicitly specifies L-cysteine·H2O·HCl; JCM553 and627 inherit that recipe with named changes that do not alter this component. The six frozen spellings retain L configuration, hydrochloride and one water. CHEBI91248 independently describes that exact form, so a typed raw alias on the active hydrate owner is justified.',None),
10:('unresolved','NBRC1116 and TOGO M2371 say EDTA sodium salt without specifying sodium stoichiometry or hydration. Current Na2-EDTA and tetrasodium tetrahydrate owners are distinct substances. Neither the use as a chelator nor surrounding trace salts chooses a form.', 'Recover the EDTA supplier/CAS or explicit Na count and hydration from NBRC1116 and the original nitrosolobus formulation; resolve the two occurrences separately if forms differ.'),
11:('stock_product_mixture_context','TOGO M2570 adds a 2.5% L-cysteine hydrochloride stock; that percentage-qualified preparation is not the pure CHEBI91247 salt or generic hydrate solution. The flat source has replaced a volume contribution by G_PER_L. The accessible source name does not state the percent basis or hydrate.', 'Verify the original ATCC stock preparation, percent basis (w/v or w/w), solvent and hydrate status before proposing a quantitatively defined stock.'),
12:('unresolved','JCM520 and95 confirm Sodium L-malate, retaining the L stereochemical qualifier. They do not state sodium stoichiometry or hydrate. Current Sodium_Malate is specifically disodium(S)-malate and also carries contradictory DL aliases; that owner defect must not supply missing source identity evidence.', 'Identify monosodium versus disodium salt and supplied hydration for both JCM recipes; independently remove misleading DL aliases from the L owner without assigning these source cases by convention.'),
13:('unresolved','TOGO M3149 confirms the unspecific cysteine-hydrochloride label but no stereochemistry or hydrate. Live issue905 documents that similarly unspecific MediaDive metadata conflicts among DL anhydrous and L hydrate identifiers. The frozen obsolete MediaIngredientMech numeric reference is not identity authority.', 'Obtain original DSM135 formulation or supplier/CAS establishing stereochemistry and water content; do not inherit either CHEBI91247 or91248 from an unspecific alias.'),
14:('stock_product_mixture_context','TOGO M2554 identifies Basal Medium as the seawater/peptone/yeast/mineral preparation dispensed in 6 ml aliquots. It explicitly excludes sodium sulfide at the preparation step and uses separately supplied powdered sulfur. The frozen 6 G_PER_L is not a concentration. Propose the named basal preparation with only constituents actually retained in that preparation.',None),
15:('unresolved','The frozen MEDIADB479 AMS1 pyruvate/glycine recipe names Sodium Phosphite at 0.001 mM. Neither the frozen component nor the attempted primary database retrieval specifies mono/disodium protonation or hydrate. The existing dibasic pentahydrate is not an exact identity established by this label.', 'Recover the AMS1 original formulation or catalogue/CAS resolving sodium/proton stoichiometry and hydration; the MediaDB479 endpoint was attempted but unavailable.'),
16:('unresolved','Both frozen yeast-mineral-medium records already contain a content-bound scientific hold: the 1992 source prints NaMoO4.2H2O, while a later formulation has Na2MoO4.2H2O. Their source notes explicitly prohibit repairing the sodium count or borrowing the later article. A failed new paper retrieval does not weaken that hold.', 'Resolve the printed 1992 one-sodium formula through an erratum or original authors’ material specification; retain source mass and unverified database molarity separately.'),
17:('stock_product_mixture_context','TOGO M2885 places 0.1M HCl as a 1 L solvent input to its trace-element stock and explicitly records conc_value0.1/conc_unitM. It is a reagent solution, not 1 g/L HCl. Propose a source-qualified 0.1 M hydrochloric-acid solution with no pure-compound equivalence.',None),
18:('stock_product_mixture_context','JCM1051 explicitly names 0.1 M L-cysteine·HCl·H2O, added as 10 ml from an anaerobic stock. Its exact solute form is supported by CHEBI91248; the complete named input is a solution. Preserve molarity and the volume contribution, not the frozen 10 G_PER_L interpretation.',None),
19:('existing_identity_or_alias','TOGO M2575 retains explicit L-cysteine hydrochloride monohydrate in its cysteine/sulfide reducing solution. Membership inside a stock does not make this component the whole stock. The source string preserves L configuration and one water and matches CHEBI91248, supporting a raw-form alias only.',None),
20:('stock_product_mixture_context','NBRC1507 specifies a 0.1 M Tris/HCl buffer at pH7.5. That buffered preparation is not pure Tris base or Tris hydrochloride. A source-qualified buffer record can retain the declared molarity/pH while leaving the unreported acid/base recipe ratio and solvent detail unasserted.',None),
21:('stock_product_mixture_context','TOGO M2596 uses 1M HCl in the sludge-fluid preparation. The source is a concentration-qualified hydrochloric acid reagent; the variable addition is not a fixed concentration in the final medium. Propose a source-qualified reagent identity, preserving source-use context.',None),
22:('existing_identity_or_alias','JCM552,627,1098,707 and757 explicitly name L-sodium lactate. All seven frozen occurrences retain L stereochemistry; nesting in JCM757 substrate solution changes use context, not the supplied solute. CHEBI232798 is sodium L-lactate. Add the exact double-hyphen spelling and reject the existing D,L synonym on the L owner.',None),
23:('stock_product_mixture_context','JCM87 actually specifies a 20% lactic-acid titrant as one alternative to hydrochloric acid, used to reach pH5.6. The frozen unqualified label omits the stock strength and alternative-use condition. Do not map this whole source occurrence to a pure lactic-acid enantiomer.', 'Recover the percent basis, acid stereochemistry and supplied solution specification for the JCM87 titrant before minting a quantitative stock or selecting a pure solute identity.'),
24:('stock_product_mixture_context','DSMZ600 gives the full artificial-seawater salt recipe and uses 250 ml of it. Its explicit constituent list differs from a generic seawater concept and is independent of the Hutner stock in the same medium. Propose a source-qualified seawater mixture retaining literal hydration and quantities.',None),
25:('stock_product_mixture_context','Both occurrences retain a 1 N NaOH reagent used to dissolve haemin before dilution. DSMZ330 provides the exact 1 ml reagent input; MediaDiveP2 notes explicitly refuse converting it to a pure-solid concentration. A stock record preserves normality without asserting an inferred molarity or final-medium NaOH amount.',None),
26:('stock_product_mixture_context','The TOGO M2228 primary record recovers Basal broth as a five-part preparation: yeast extract, phenol-red solution, bacitracin, meticillin and Solution1. Solution1 itself includes BHI, PPLO broth and Hanks salts; this is not equivalent to BHI alone. Propose an exact source-qualified complex stock and keep raw input amounts without an inferred final-volume denominator.',None),
27:('stock_product_mixture_context','DSMZ600 delegates Hutner salts to DSMZ590. The recovered DSMZ590 recipe is an NTA/mineral mixture with Metals44 and acid/base adjustment, not JCM631 Hunter salts. Its molybdate row is printed (NH4)6MoO7O24 x4H2O, so exact chemical component identity is unresolved even though the nominal recipe is recovered.', 'An authoritative correction or product specification for the malformed molybdate component in DSMZ590 is needed before a chemically exact stock decomposition; preserve all original ingredients and pH adjustments.'),
28:('unresolved','NBRC1022 explicitly lists Sodium tetrathionate 2 g. This establishes the sodium salt family, not free tetrathionate ion identity or a particular hydrate. The existing Na-tetrathionate placeholder should not be promoted by substituting the ion owner.', 'Resolve sodium tetrathionate supplied hydration/CAS and exact ontology availability from an original NBRC1022 material specification; preserve the current unmapped sodium-salt owner meanwhile.'),
29:('unresolved','TOGO M2598 confirms Cysteine HCl xH2O but the name and available recipe text do not establish L versus DL. CHEBI91248 is L specific. A one-water suffix resolves hydration but cannot resolve stereochemistry.', 'Obtain supplier/CAS or explicit stereochemical wording for the cysteine hydrochloride monohydrate in ATCC Methanogenium medium.'),
30:('broad_parent_relation_only','TOGO M2313 lists citrus-peel pectin as one alternative carbon-source material. Citrus tissue origin is meaningful product scope; the generic CHEBI17309 Pectin record does not establish a supplier product or esterification preparation. Retain a broader pectin link only as a candidate, with no exact source alias.', 'A source/product-bound material decision is needed for citrus-peel pectin before an exact MIM owner is assigned; do not collapse it with apple pectin or generic polysaccharide from the same alternatives list.'),
31:('unresolved','NBRC1397 states magnesium glycerophosphate at 0.5 g without positional isomer, hydration or a supplier specification. Glycerophosphate salts can differ by isomer and hydrate; sodium-glycerophosphate issues1118/1053 illustrate why a formula family is not an exact product identity and do not decide this magnesium case.', 'Recover the magnesium salt’s positional-isomer composition, stoichiometry and hydration or catalogue/CAS from the NBRC1397 source.'),
32:('stock_product_mixture_context','Sigma A9647 is bovine serum albumin, currently described as heat-shock fraction, pH7, lyophilized powder; the three recipes call it fractionV in OADC stock. The maintained Bovine_Serum_Albumin record already preserves A9647 as a source-specific supplied form and explicitly forbids making fraction/product names exact generic synonyms. Preserve that prior ruling.',None),
33:('unresolved','The five occurrences print two ammoniums with a dodecahydrate. DSMZ1165 instead prints Fe(NH4)(SO4)2 x12H2O (ferric ammonium sulfate), while DSMZ1148 still prints the two-ammonium formula. The change affects charge/oxidation and hydrate identity. No single exact salt can be inferred for the aggregate spelling.', 'Resolve each DSMZ1148/1165 and MediaDive1036 source against an authoritative material specification or correction; distinguish ferric ammonium sulfate dodecahydrate from ferrous ammonium sulfate forms.'),
34:('malformed_or_nonchemical_token','NBRC1196 makes Substrates* a parameter and explains examples as vanillic acid and syringic acid etc. It is neither one substance nor a fixed mixture. Source-specific medium variants or an explicit selectable-substrate relation are required, not an ingredient identity.',None),
35:('stock_product_mixture_context','JCM979 provides Hutner salts and Metals44 but prints (NH4)6MoO24·4H2O, omitting the molybdenum count. Its Mg and Ca quantities differ from JCM631 Hunter stock. Retain the nominal stock boundary without repairing that chemically consequential formula or equating the names.', 'Obtain a JCM979 correction/product identity for the molybdate component and confirm the Metals44 substock before asserting a chemically exact reusable stock.'),
36:('unresolved','TOGO M3140 names NTA (sodium nitrilotriacetate), so the free acid is not an exact candidate. The label does not choose mono/disodium versus trisodium or a hydrate. Existing trisodium and disodium NTA owners are comparison candidates only.', 'Resolve sodium stoichiometry and hydrate of the M3140 NTA material using source catalogue/CAS or explicit formula; do not choose trisodium monohydrate from abbreviation alone.'),
37:('unresolved','NBRC302 and305 both retain Na2MoO3·2H2O, rather than the Na2MoO4·2H2O formula of CHEBI75213. The four frozen occurrences inherit this source-level formula conflict and milligram-to-gram flattening. Oxygen count cannot be silently repaired as lexical normalization.', 'An NBRC correction, original recipe or supplier/CAS must establish whether the MoO3 label denotes molybdate or another compound; preserve the exact O3 source spelling meanwhile.'),
38:('stock_product_mixture_context','JCM900 recovers Modified Hutner salts with NTA, minerals and Metals44, but the molybdate row is (NH4)6MoO24·4H2O. This nominal recipe must remain separate from JCM631 and the vitamin solution also printed on the page. A safe exact chemical formulation requires resolution of the malformed molybdate component.', 'Resolve the molybdenum stoichiometry in JCM900’s own recipe; a spelling similarity to another Hutner stock cannot supply the missing atom count.'),
39:('unresolved','The frozen source says sodium dithionate, which differs from sodium dithionite by oxygen content and cannot be corrected merely because dithionite is a familiar reducing agent. The direct JCM876 page currently returns Nothing found; the historical TOGO record and its source wording must be retained.', 'Recover the original JCM876 formulation or supplier/CAS distinguishing dithionate from dithionite before selecting either chemical identity.'),
40:('stock_product_mixture_context','TOGO M3115 uses 0.1 M HCl as the solvent for the trace-element solution. This is the acid reagent before trace metals are added, not the complete trace-metal stock or pure HCl. Preserve its source-qualified reagent boundary and declared strength.',None),
41:('existing_identity_or_alias','JCM704 and the frozen JCM833 lineage name sodium citrate dihydrate. CHEBI32142 uses that same chemical name for trisodium citrate dihydrate. The two-water qualification is explicit and retained; add the exact punctuation spelling to the active Na3-citrate dihydrate owner, never to anhydrous citrate.',None),
42:('stock_product_mixture_context','All three DSMZ cell-culture recipes add 0.5 ml of a 100x amino-acid stock to a 50.5 ml batch. CHEBI33709 amino acid is a class and not the whole mixture. The recovered recipes do not enumerate amino acids or identify a catalogue formulation, so neither one amino acid nor an arbitrary commercial blend is justified.', 'Identify the supplier/catalogue and constituent formulation of the 100x amino-acid stock used in DSMZ1193,1198 and1503; verify whether the same product was intended in all three.'),
43:('unresolved','NBRC1333 explicitly prints Na2MoO4·4H2O in a 1000x stock. The formula names four waters, not the existing dihydrate CHEBI75213. Its recipe amount is 0.1 g in 100 ml, not necessarily the frozen final-medium concentration. Preserve the four-water claim until the actual reagent is established.', 'Obtain the original NBRC1333 molybdate reagent specification/CAS or an erratum resolving the tetrahydrate; do not reuse the dihydrate by convention.'),
44:('supplied_form_correction','The CCAP Walnes primary PDF clearly prints MnCl2.4H2O in the nutrient stock; the frozen token MnCl .4H 0 has lost subscripts and letter O. Correct this exact source occurrence to manganese(II) chloride tetrahydrate while retaining the malformed token as extraction provenance; do not create an active malformed alias.',None),
45:('stock_product_mixture_context','TOGO M2653 identifies 25% sodium acetate as a separate stock addition in methanogen medium, not pure sodium acetate. The frozen amount4 is detached from its volume unit. The name alone does not state w/v versus w/w or whether the amount is based on a hydrated starting reagent.', 'Recover the original ATCC percent-basis and preparation for the 25% sodium acetate stock before a quantitative exact formulation proposal.'),
46:('stock_product_mixture_context','NBRC989 uses 25 ml of 50% sodium lactate; the two frozen occurrences disagree by ML_PER_L versus G_PER_L for the same source. The stock is distinct from the pure salt and lacks explicit percentage basis and stereochemistry. Preserve the unit conflict rather than averaging or deduplicating amounts.', 'Verify NBRC989 supplied product/stereochemistry and percentage basis; correct the TOGO-derived G_PER_L occurrence from the primary ml quantity before mapping the stock.'),
47:('stock_product_mixture_context','JCM1429 explicitly delegates this stock to JCM900, establishing a recipe link rather than a generic synonym. The linked source has an unresolved molybdate formula. Preserve the reference to900 and use the same chemical-resolution obligation as case38, not a link to JCM631 Hunter salts.', 'Resolve JCM900’s malformed molybdate component and retain the exact JCM1429→900 stock reference before integration.'),
48:('stock_product_mixture_context','TOGO M2616 identifies ComponentII as a separately prepared phosphate portion of modified Baar medium. The ordinal label is local to this formulation and cannot be a global synonym for phosphate or another ComponentII. Propose the exact source-qualified substock using its captured subcomponent table.',None),
49:('stock_product_mixture_context','TOGO M2215 explicitly specifies salmon sperm DNA from Sigma. This preserves organism/tissue and supplier scope; neither generic DNA nor the herring-sperm alias in Fish-sperm_Dna establishes equivalent material. The maintained DNA_From_Salmon CAS record also lacks proof it denotes this exact sperm-derived supplier product.', 'Recover the Sigma catalogue identifier or original material specification before equating this preparation with an existing salmon DNA owner; retain tissue origin and supplier meanwhile.'),
50:('stock_product_mixture_context','The eighteen occurrences retain fat-free ground beef, but come from DSMZ/ATCC/JCM chopped-meat formulations and normalized KOMODO variants. The primary recipes include meat processing and possible tissue substitutions. These heterogeneous tissue preparations must not collapse to beef extract or to one exact processed product from spelling alone.', 'Compare the original meat preparation and any allowed substitution per occurrence before assigning a single supplied-material identity; retain the three KOMODO-derived concentration values independently.'),
51:('existing_identity_or_alias','JCM1331 titanium-citrate stock and JCM1492 iron stock explicitly use sodium citrate·2H2O. The solid input is sodium citrate dihydrate CHEBI32142, not the resulting titanium/iron solution. Add the exact spelling only; source amount/final-volume discrepancies belong to recipe correction, not identity.',None),
52:('existing_identity_or_alias','Both source occurrences explicitly say Cyanocobalamin, with VitaminB12 as a parenthetical gloss. CCAP stock4 and NBRC1550 support this named vitamer; the frozen CHEBI176843 class on one occurrence is broader than the explicit compound. CHEBI17439 is the matching cyanocobalamin identity. Add only this fully qualified alias, not generic VitaminB12.',None),
53:('unresolved','TOGO M3213 names sodium monobasic phosphate but does not state a hydrate or supplier. The source establishes NaH2PO4 protonation but cannot choose among the anhydrous, mono- and dihydrate supplied substances represented in MIM. Preserve the source distinction rather than using a nearest label.', 'Resolve the supplied hydration/CAS in the saline basal medium; do not map to a hydrate solely from the 4.35 g source amount.'),
54:('stock_product_mixture_context','JCM554 prints sodium fumarate with an instruction to adjust pH7.0. The label includes preparation, and the primary gives neither a separate stock volume nor sodium stoichiometry. Treat the instruction as recipe context; no global active alias for the whole prepared string on disodium fumarate.', 'Identify whether the source used supplied mono/disodium fumarate or prepared sodium fumarate by neutralization, and retain the pH adjustment in the recipe owner.'),
55:('new_distinct_ingredient_proposal','JCM1107 and1355 explicitly specify nitrilotriacetic acid trisodium salt monohydrate; MediaDive1930 corroborates the source product. CHEBI132766 describes the water-free trisodium salt, so this hydrate needs its distinct identity. Share primary_c’s reviewed promotion of existing Na3-NTA_X_H2O; do not mint a duplicate owner.',None),
56:('new_distinct_ingredient_proposal','Sigma’s exact D1501 product is calf-thymus DNA sodium salt, TypeI fibrous material. TOGO M2785 names the same catalogue code, establishing supplier/tissue/salt scope. The product is heterogeneous biological DNA and not fish-sperm DNA or generic deoxyribonucleic acid. Propose a source-qualified biological preparation with supplier metadata, no invented whole-material structure.',None),
57:('unresolved','JCM566’s direct page is unavailable, while the frozen TOGO M570 component explicitly retains DL sodium malate. This racemate cannot be an exact alias on Sodium_Malate CHEBI91261 (S-specific). CHEBI91260 disodium malate is a comparison candidate but the source still lacks sodium stoichiometry.', 'Recover the M570/JCM566 supplied salt stoichiometry/hydration; preserve DL and do not infer disodium or L identity from existing mixed owner synonyms.'),
58:('malformed_or_nonchemical_token','NiCI2.6H2O uses uppercase I where a chloride formula would use lowercase l; nearby MnCI2 andCoCI2 show the same character-loss pattern. TOGO’s own component annotation identifies nickel chloride hexahydrate, supporting an extraction-error hypothesis, not a new iodide/chloride species. Preserve the token as rejected provenance pending source correction.', 'Verify the original Pfennig-medium printed reagent before correcting the exact occurrence to NiCl2·6H2O; do not publish the damaged token as a universal alias.'),
59:('stock_product_mixture_context','TOGO M866 names 1.0 M sodium lactate as a separate solution. JCM830’s direct page is now unavailable, so the source-qualified nominal stock can preserve the TOGO specification without choosing L versus DL from the existing owner. No exact pure-salt link is proposed.',None),
60:('unresolved','NaII CO3 is not a usable neutral sodium-carbonate formula. Replacing II with H or2 changes bicarbonate versus carbonate identity; both are plausible media components. TOGO’s annotation is a useful lead but cannot independently repair the damaged original formula.', 'Recover the original YPS mineral-base recipe or supplier/CAS establishing bicarbonate versus carbonate for this exact NaII CO3 occurrence.'),
61:('existing_identity_or_alias','DSMZ1094 explicitly lists MES acid in SolutionC alongside separately added NaOH. The component’s acid name matches CHEBI39005; the mixed buffer is not the same entity. Add the exact expanded MES spelling to its existing acid owner while preserving the separate buffer-preparation context.',None),
62:('stock_product_mixture_context','JCM579 adds 0.2 ml of filter-sterilized1.0 M sodium acetate per10 ml medium. The frozen0.2G_PER_L is a flattened source quantity, not the stock composition. Propose the source-qualified1M reagent and preserve filtration as preparation metadata.',None),
63:('unresolved','Kaminskyj’s primary trace-element table explicitly says Na4EDTA5g, followed by adjustment to100ml. It therefore establishes tetrasodium stoichiometry but not hydration. The existing tetrasodium tetrahydrate owner adds four waters absent from the source; no exact alias to it is justified.', 'Identify the Na4EDTA supplied hydrate/CAS for the Kaminskyj stock before selecting anhydrous, dihydrate or tetrahydrate; the50g/L stock calculation alone cannot choose.'),
64:('unresolved','Eight MediaDB occurrences say sodium borate with different media and millimolar amounts. That label does not establish borate stoichiometry or water content; existing borate ion, borax decahydrate and other salts are chemically different. The Song recipe evidence explicitly limits itself to database quantity, not supplied form.', 'Recover original compound specifications for the Deshpande, Lostroh, MR andSong source families; determine borate stoichiometry and hydration separately before grouping their identical labels.'),
65:('stock_product_mixture_context','JCM537 lists65mg hemin within its cofactor solution and says it is separately dissolved in10mM NaOH. The volume of that initial solvent and final hemin concentration are not given. Neither the entire label nor the cofactor stock is pure hemin; the frozen65G_PER_L also loses the mg unit.', 'Recover the separate hemin-in-NaOH preparation volume and form before defining that stock; correct source65mg versus frozen65G_PER_L without assuming a1L hemin substock.'),
66:('stock_product_mixture_context','TOGO M3265 uses2M HCl to adjust the iron/sulfur-free basal medium. The exact declared reagent strength can be preserved as a source-qualified hydrochloric-acid stock, with variable titrant amount kept in recipe context and no pure-HCl equivalence.',None),
67:('unresolved','JCM788 itself prints K2HSO4, and the four frozen derivatives preserve it. Ordinary K+ andHSO4− do not neutralize at this2:1 ratio; KHSO4, K2SO4 andK2HPO4 would be different corrections. The use as a buffer does not decide the intended salt.', 'Obtain JCM788 erratum/original material specification resolving the extra potassium/proton or sulfur/phosphorus error; do not silently select phosphate or sulfate.'),
68:('unresolved','The two TAP recipes assert Cobalt ion with CHEBI48828 cobalt(2+) but report only a database concentration. An ion concentration is not the identity of the salt or stock used to supply it. The available source context does not independently establish oxidation state or counterion; preserve the ion assertion as source metadata.', 'Inspect the original TAP trace-element formulation to establish cobalt oxidation state and supplied salt/hydrate; keep database ion concentration separate from any whole-reagent identity.'),
69:('new_distinct_ingredient_proposal','JCM1481 explicitly names Sigma-Aldrich Bold Modified Basal Freshwater Nutrient Solution50x at20ml. Sigma B5282’s primary product page identifies the same named50x liquid stock and20ml/L use rate. Propose a product-qualified stock identity; it is neither the final1x medium nor an individual mineral.',None),
}
