ASSESSMENTS[15]=('unresolved','MediaDB479 was recovered through the web tool and links Carini2014 (doi:10.1038/ncomms5346). Its Methods/Cultivation details explicitly name phosphite as NaPHO3·5H2O. This resolves five waters but the printed one-sodium formula differs from the maintained dibasic pentahydrate; do not silently insert a second sodium. The source concentration1µM is consistent with0.001mM, independently of salt identity.', 'Obtain a correction or supplier/CAS resolving the printed NaPHO3·5H2O sodium/proton stoichiometry in Carini2014; keep the pentahydrate and original formula explicit.')
ASSESSMENTS[68]=('unresolved','The two MediaDB TAP records represent cobalt as an ion concentration with CHEBI48828. The Chlamydomonas Resource Center TAP recipe links Hutner trace elements, which explicitly contains CoCl2·6H2O1.61g/L and is added1ml/L; this is compatible with approximately0.0068mM cobalt. That comparative recipe supports a cobalt(II) supplier-salt lead but does not show the exact2009 source used this variant, and an ion inventory is not the whole hexahydrate reagent.', 'Verify the exact trace-element recipe used by the2009 MediaDB36/37 study and preserve an explicit ion-to-supplied-salt relationship; do not replace Cobalt ion with cobalt chloride hexahydrate as exact identity.')
